@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Edit fields, assignment, dates, and status
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "WorkItemDetailPage or WorkHierarchyPage / WorkItemFormDialog / WorkItemForm, or WorkItemDetailView" as page
  participant "IWorkItemService / WorkItemService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "WorkItemsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "UpdateWorkItemCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "WorkItem" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
alt Edit form
  actor -> page : Edit on an item (the view's actionRequested); the page opens WorkItemFormDialog
  page -> client : WorkItemForm's workItemResource reads GetWorkItemQuery; fields and Save stay disabled (edit-loading)
  alt Read fails (500 or 503 with correlation ID, or no response)
    client --> page : Fields stay disabled; alert with Try again = reload(), Cancel, and the reference ID only when the server answered (edit-load-failed)
  else Read 404: the item was deleted after the page loaded
    client --> page : Fields and Save stay disabled; "no longer exists" with Back to work, no reference ID or Try again (edit-not-found); Back to work emits notFound, the dialog closes with NotFound, and the page calls the layout's refresh() (the detail page opens the work outline)
  else Item read
    client --> page : The draft starts from the resolved values; draftChange reports a clean draft
  end
  opt Cancel, Close, or Escape with a dirty draft
    page -> page : UnsavedChangesDialog asks first; Keep editing returns with every value; Discard closes and sends nothing
  end
  actor -> page : Edit fields, assignment (searchable active-people combobox; see the assignee sequence), dates, or status and save
  page -> client : Disable Save while pending; draftChange reports pending (L2-031); build typed UpdateWorkItemCommand (explicit nulls for cleared fields, expected item version)
else Status control or task-row status select on the detail
  actor -> page : Choose a status other than Done for a story, or any status for another item
  page -> client : setStatus: UpdateWorkItemCommand with only the status and that item's version; absent fields stay unchanged
  note right of page : Outcomes are in Create and navigate: success reloads the detail and children and announces; a stale 409 reloads them once; 500 or 503 shows status-failed (under a task's row)
end
client -> access : PUT /api/workspaces/{id}/work-items/{itemId}
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the promise rejects with its 401 (nothing written); sign-in shows session-unsaved when a draft was dirty, then returns to the item
else Authenticated active account (profile P: editing work needs no capability beyond an active session)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send UpdateWorkItemCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-016 title 1-200, description up to 10,000, known status, calendar dates, estimate a whole number of 0 or more (the command carries no item type and may leave a date absent, so the type and date-order checks wait for the handler)
  alt Invalid fields
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read or changed
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Keep every value; one field error moves focus to that field, which reads its error; several focus the linked error summary (validation state); no Retry or reference ID
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle UpdateWorkItemCommand
    handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync takes the workspace lock first; then LoadWorkItemAsync, or LoadStoryPlacementsAsync for a story status change; LoadAccountStatusAsync for a newly chosen assignee; a task status change also loads its parent story
    db --> handler : Current item and reference state, or lock-wait timeout
    alt Workspace lock wait times out
      handler --> ctrl : 503 with Retry-After; nothing read or changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (unavailable)
      client --> page : Unavailable save, as for a 500: keep every value; "We couldn't save this story" with reference ID; focus stays on Save, which resends only when chosen (failed state)
    else Workspace or item not found
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : Edit form: edit-not-found, as for a read 404. Status control or task row: the detail and children reread once; a deleted task leaves the tasks list, and focus moves to the Tasks heading; for the item itself the read's 404 category decides (item-not-found: the item's not-found state; workspace-not-found: Project not found and notFound, so the page calls the layout's refresh())
    else Stale item version (L2-041)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 stale version; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (changed)
      client --> page : The promise rejects with the 409; WorkItemForm keeps the attempted values and calls reload() on its item resource once; never resubmits
      page --> actor : Compare "Your edit" with "Latest saved"; Save gives way to Reload latest, which receives focus (conflict state)
      opt Reload latest
        actor -> page : Reload latest
        page -> page : Adopt latest values and version; comparison stays visible; Save enabled; focus moves to Title (conflict-reloaded state)
      end
    else L2-016 estimate sent for an item that isn't a story; due date before start once the sent dates merge with the saved ones; or a newly chosen assignee deactivated after selection, or unknown
      handler --> ctrl : 400 field error on the estimate, the due date, or the assignee; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails (that field)
      client --> page : Keep every value; focus moves to that field, which reads its error; no Retry or reference ID (rejected state for the assignee)
    else Story set to Done with unfinished tasks; condition absent or not current
      handler -> handler : L2-021 StoryStatusTransition applies StoryCompletionPolicy: sent condition missing or not current
      handler --> ctrl : 409 unfinished-tasks with count and StoryCompletionCondition; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (unfinished-tasks)
      client --> page : WorkItemForm keeps the edit and emits completionStatus ConfirmationRequired; WorkItemFormDialog opens UnfinishedTasksDialog ("Mark a story Done from the edit form")
    else Edit permitted
      handler -> entity : L2-016 apply validated fields; keep an unchanged inactive assignee; type and workspace unchanged
      entity --> handler : Updated details
      handler -> handler : Story status change: StoryStatusTransition.apply sets the status, moves every live board placement to the new column, and increments the active sprint's version for a member (closure revision matrix). Task status change: increment the parent story's task revision only; the story's version and every sprint's version stay unchanged
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent, then SaveChangesAsync: item, placements, sprint version, story task revision, and success audit in one transaction
      alt Commit fails
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-save claim
        client --> page : Keep every value; "We couldn't save this story" with reference ID; focus stays on Save, which retries the same request only when chosen (failed state)
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : New item version
        handler --> ctrl : Updated item
        ctrl --> client : 200 with new version
        client --> page : WorkItemForm emits saved with a WorkItemSavedResult (WorkItemSaved, title, parentTitle); the dialog closes with Saved(saved, title, parentTitle)
        page --> actor : The page increments its refresh counter, so its view rereads (the detail and children, or every expanded branch); the "Changes saved" toast through TOAST_SERVICE; focus returns to Edit
      end
    end
  end
end
opt No response to the save (timeout or network failure)
  client --> page : The save may have committed. Edit form: keep the attempted values; the failed alert reads "We couldn't confirm whether your changes were saved" without a reference ID; WorkItemForm calls reload() on its item resource once and emits unconfirmed, which the dialog relays so the page rereads its view at once; Save resends only when pressed; a committed save then meets the stale 409, whose comparison reads "The latest saved version is shown beside your entries", never "Your edits haven't been saved". Status control: the detail and children reload once; status-failed says it couldn't confirm and names the persisted status, without reference ID or Try again
end
note over ctrl, db
An unexpected 403 changes nothing; the edit form keeps every value and emits forbidden (relayed by WorkItemFormDialog), or the detail view restores the saved status and emits forbidden; the routed page shows the "Your access changed" toast through TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry or reference ID; the capability refresh still runs.
Checks run in this order under the lock, before any write: item exists, version current, estimate allowed for the item's type and merged dates in order, assignee active, completion condition.
SaveChangesAsync also compares the tracked expected version; its ConcurrencyConflictException maps to the same 409.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
